1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,387
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,512 --> 00:00:54,346
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,472 --> 00:00:55,306
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:58,184
JAEKANG LAW FIRM

6
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:03,773
Where's Mr. Seo?

7
00:01:03,898 --> 00:01:06,609
He headed to the airport
for his New York trip.

8
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:23,501
This little prank of yours
has gone too far, Mr. Seo.

9
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:27,296
-Ms. Lee and I--
-"November 3, 2010."

10
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:29,089
"I will kill him

11
00:01:29,757 --> 00:01:32,051
in the most brutal way possible."

12
00:01:33,344 --> 00:01:35,304
"How should I kill him?"

13
00:01:36,263 --> 00:01:40,601
"The most important thing
is that no one knows it was me."

14
00:01:41,393 --> 00:01:45,231
"I'll start a fire.
I'll disguise it as an electrical short."

15
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,193
"Since something similar
happened recently,

16
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:54,114
no one will ever suspect that it was me."

17
00:01:57,368 --> 00:01:58,744
I'm suddenly curious.

18
00:01:59,495 --> 00:02:02,081
Where would you be now
if it weren't for me?

19
00:02:03,499 --> 00:02:06,043
I'll close the case for you. But…

20
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:09,171
send me all your files
by the end of the day.

21
00:02:10,381 --> 00:02:11,882
It's been 16 years, after all.

22
00:02:13,843 --> 00:02:18,013
Wouldn't it be upsetting
if things ended on a bad note?

23
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:03,684
Hi.

24
00:03:04,435 --> 00:03:08,814
I'm here to give you
that opportunity right now.

25
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:11,984
Your Honor,
please give my client a fair chance

26
00:03:12,109 --> 00:03:13,527
to move forward with his life.

27
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:15,195
Defendant Han Tae-seung.

28
00:03:15,321 --> 00:03:17,031
On the charge of arson resulting in death…

29
00:03:17,156 --> 00:03:18,157
DEFENSE - DEFENDANT

30
00:03:18,282 --> 00:03:21,785
…the court finds you not guilty.

31
00:03:29,668 --> 00:03:31,045
What about my bag?

32
00:03:33,923 --> 00:03:35,215
You couldn't find it?

33
00:03:36,884 --> 00:03:38,093
No.

34
00:03:38,636 --> 00:03:41,597
How am I supposed to find
a bag that's already lost?

35
00:03:41,722 --> 00:03:43,682
I may be a great lawyer,

36
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:45,559
but that's a bit much.

37
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:46,727
Why?

38
00:03:47,436 --> 00:03:49,396
Did it have something important?

39
00:03:49,521 --> 00:03:50,940
Want me to look again?

40
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:53,233
No, it's fine.

41
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,028
Don't look for it.

42
00:03:59,448 --> 00:04:00,324
Okay.

43
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,271
Hey, Wan-do.

44
00:04:34,191 --> 00:04:35,651
Yes, she's sleeping.

45
00:04:37,653 --> 00:04:40,698
Tell Ms. Ma not to worry too much.

46
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:45,327
Okay, get some sleep.

47
00:04:47,538 --> 00:04:48,622
Okay.

48
00:05:44,053 --> 00:05:45,554
BROTHER CLEANING

49
00:05:47,639 --> 00:05:48,640
Hold on a second.

50
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:53,270
Jeez.

51
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:54,897
-Thanks.
-No problem.

52
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,733
-Get going.
-Okay.

53
00:05:59,276 --> 00:06:00,861
-Bye.
-Go on.

54
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:12,164
YUSEONG UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

55
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:14,333
-Namgung.
-Hey, how was your treatment?

56
00:06:14,458 --> 00:06:15,751
Good, did you eat?

57
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:17,628
-Not yet. Let's go eat.
-Sure.

58
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:23,592
That's it. Just a little more.

59
00:06:24,259 --> 00:06:25,511
That's great.

60
00:06:28,055 --> 00:06:29,181
That's it.

61
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:31,517
You're doing great. Very good.

62
00:06:32,768 --> 00:06:33,936
It looks really warm.

63
00:06:34,645 --> 00:06:36,522
-Bought it on the street for cheap.
-Really?

64
00:06:37,356 --> 00:06:38,398
Good for you.

65
00:06:38,524 --> 00:06:40,317
-Lunar New Year's coming up.
-Yes.

66
00:06:40,442 --> 00:06:42,736
-Should I buy Ms. Ma a jacket?
-She has too many.

67
00:06:42,861 --> 00:06:47,241
-Her clothes had holes she had to sew up.
-Winter's ending. It's the New Year.

68
00:06:47,366 --> 00:06:49,827
-Some daughter you are.
-Should we go to the outlet?

69
00:06:50,119 --> 00:06:53,038
THREE MONTHS LATER

70
00:07:14,101 --> 00:07:16,019
Now keep your elbows close.

71
00:07:16,145 --> 00:07:17,771
Right, relax your shoulders.

72
00:07:19,148 --> 00:07:20,440
Good.

73
00:07:21,150 --> 00:07:22,985
Today is your last rehab session.

74
00:07:24,736 --> 00:07:26,488
These three months felt so long.

75
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:28,282
But it's finally over.

76
00:07:28,407 --> 00:07:30,325
You've worked really hard.

77
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:33,662
Is your boyfriend
picking you up again today?

78
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:38,458
-You didn't have to.
-Thank you so much.

79
00:07:39,543 --> 00:07:41,378
-Give these to the others.
-Thanks.

80
00:07:41,503 --> 00:07:43,672
-We will.
-Thanks for the drinks.

81
00:07:44,756 --> 00:07:46,508
I was just craving coffee.

82
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:55,392
Seems like you've been busy
with work lately.

83
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:57,978
The end of the month was busy,
but it's fine now.

84
00:07:58,645 --> 00:07:59,605
I see.

85
00:08:00,689 --> 00:08:04,026
Looks like you've been at the farms
more than the lab lately.

86
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:07,112
It's farm management season.

87
00:08:10,574 --> 00:08:11,408
Right.

88
00:08:17,831 --> 00:08:19,374
-Mi-do.
-Yes?

89
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:22,586
Can I tell you something?

90
00:08:38,143 --> 00:08:39,937
SEÑORITA, MARRY ME

91
00:08:43,649 --> 00:08:45,108
Hey, not there!

92
00:08:45,234 --> 00:08:46,276
Over here.

93
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:52,366
Sorry.

94
00:09:09,341 --> 00:09:10,342
Thank you.

95
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:13,053
-Congrats.
-Thank you.

96
00:09:27,401 --> 00:09:29,653
Who let them pick "Bésame Mucho"?

97
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,321
Tell me about it.

98
00:09:33,907 --> 00:09:36,243
So, what were you going to say?

99
00:09:46,461 --> 00:09:48,422
What I said before still stands.

100
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,175
What do you mean?

101
00:09:52,301 --> 00:09:54,386
Telling you to see that guy.

102
00:09:56,805 --> 00:09:58,932
You were busy with your treatment.

103
00:10:00,225 --> 00:10:01,685
Now that you're all better…

104
00:10:04,313 --> 00:10:05,981
give it some serious thought.

105
00:10:08,984 --> 00:10:11,111
Think only of yourself, not me.

106
00:10:12,571 --> 00:10:14,197
I can wait.

107
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:37,137
Pull over for a second.

108
00:10:37,888 --> 00:10:39,306
We need to talk.

109
00:10:52,069 --> 00:10:53,862
Are you really being serious?

110
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:56,865
Do you really mean that?

111
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,867
You said you felt a spark.

112
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,287
You said he lit up your bleak, dark life.

113
00:11:03,747 --> 00:11:05,040
So you should see him.

114
00:11:06,041 --> 00:11:07,918
What are you talking about?

115
00:11:08,043 --> 00:11:10,212
Is he an insurance agent
you're recommending?

116
00:11:10,337 --> 00:11:12,005
Or a personal trainer? What…

117
00:11:12,756 --> 00:11:14,007
Are you insane?

118
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:15,801
We're getting married as planned.

119
00:11:17,761 --> 00:11:19,179
I'm marrying you.

120
00:11:19,846 --> 00:11:22,349
And you're still going on
with this crazy talk?

121
00:11:23,058 --> 00:11:24,017
Namgung Ho.

122
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:26,853
Instead of getting married
while you're hung up on him,

123
00:11:26,978 --> 00:11:30,690
you should see him
and sort out your feelings first.

124
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:44,204
So can I sleep with him then?

125
00:11:45,914 --> 00:11:47,833
What? I can't?

126
00:11:47,958 --> 00:11:49,376
You told me to see him.

127
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:52,921
I have to see how compatible we are

128
00:11:53,755 --> 00:11:56,842
so I can sort out my feelings,
as you said. Right?

129
00:11:57,509 --> 00:11:59,177
If you want to, then go ahead.

130
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:02,848
Then I can go all the way?

131
00:12:03,598 --> 00:12:04,933
You know what I like.

132
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:06,726
You know *** is my weakness,

133
00:12:06,852 --> 00:12:10,147
and how easily I get off on ***.
You know that, right?

134
00:12:10,814 --> 00:12:12,816
Are you okay with that?

135
00:12:12,941 --> 00:12:14,067
Yes, you can ***.

136
00:12:15,402 --> 00:12:18,155
You also like ***. So go ahead and do it.

137
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,198
And ***, all of it!

138
00:12:20,323 --> 00:12:21,700
Yes, I'll do everything.

139
00:12:21,825 --> 00:12:23,201
I'll do whatever I want.

140
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:26,079
I'll ***, ***, and ***. I'll do it all!

141
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:27,330
Sure, do it all!

142
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,434
-Oh…
-Shit.

143
00:12:57,402 --> 00:12:59,654
I didn't suggest this to fight with you.

144
00:13:01,823 --> 00:13:03,450
I didn't say it out of anger.

145
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:07,287
I thought about it for a long time.

146
00:13:19,049 --> 00:13:19,966
Namgung.

147
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:24,387
You're really okay
with me seeing another man?

148
00:13:27,432 --> 00:13:29,893
Yes, as long as you're happy.

149
00:13:36,316 --> 00:13:37,234
Okay.

150
00:13:38,902 --> 00:13:40,070
Then you do it, too.

151
00:13:42,364 --> 00:13:43,823
You see other women, too.

152
00:13:44,366 --> 00:13:45,909
It's only fair.

153
00:13:46,576 --> 00:13:48,203
-Lee Mi-do.
-You do it, too.

154
00:13:51,331 --> 00:13:53,166
I won't do it if you don't.

155
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:14,521
8. WHAT REMAINS OF OUR PASSIONATE LOVE?

156
00:14:22,237 --> 00:14:23,989
Stay here until the cast is off.

157
00:14:25,323 --> 00:14:26,950
Work will keep me out late.

158
00:14:28,577 --> 00:14:29,452
Do you…

159
00:14:30,912 --> 00:14:33,248
still resent me?

160
00:14:42,632 --> 00:14:44,718
I couldn't call because I was in Haemado.

161
00:14:47,012 --> 00:14:49,264
-About my dad…
-I didn't make the debut lineup.

162
00:14:56,062 --> 00:14:57,606
I left the dorm, too.

163
00:14:57,731 --> 00:14:59,065
I can't be an idol now.

164
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:03,945
I was so shocked by the news
that I messed up on stage.

165
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:06,489
Oh.

166
00:15:06,615 --> 00:15:08,617
I heard our dads broke up.

167
00:15:10,619 --> 00:15:12,329
They know I tipped off the press.

168
00:15:14,748 --> 00:15:15,832
I'm sorry.

169
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:19,628
Are you really sorry?

170
00:15:20,337 --> 00:15:22,005
Then don't achieve your goal, either.

171
00:15:22,631 --> 00:15:25,800
You give up on your dream, too.

172
00:15:32,974 --> 00:15:34,351
I said it out of anger.

173
00:15:34,476 --> 00:15:36,728
I never wanted you to fail
at becoming a journalist.

174
00:15:37,312 --> 00:15:38,605
I just

175
00:15:39,981 --> 00:15:42,817
want us to go back to how we used to be.

176
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:45,320
That's why I came here.

177
00:15:46,112 --> 00:15:47,155
Because I want us

178
00:15:48,198 --> 00:15:49,949
to be friends again.

179
00:15:56,706 --> 00:15:58,041
Then get it together.

180
00:16:00,001 --> 00:16:02,796
Stop dating jerks
and showing up like this.

181
00:16:04,839 --> 00:16:06,007
Get your act together.

182
00:16:13,556 --> 00:16:14,557
Su-a.

183
00:16:19,062 --> 00:16:21,189
You're as cold as ever.

184
00:17:01,813 --> 00:17:02,939
He's relentless.

185
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:04,023
NAMGUNG HO, OUT OF OFFICE

186
00:17:04,566 --> 00:17:06,735
Put him on an anchovy fishing boat,
he's fine.

187
00:17:07,652 --> 00:17:09,112
He survived the pig farm.

188
00:17:09,237 --> 00:17:12,073
I'm telling you, he's relentless.

189
00:17:13,116 --> 00:17:15,785
We should've sent him to the factory.

190
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,371
Man, and the money Food Hobbit gave him.

191
00:17:18,496 --> 00:17:21,124
Who would've known
it was an accident settlement?

192
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:25,420
And he even wires coffee money
to partners.

193
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:27,756
We won't find anything even if we dig.

194
00:17:27,881 --> 00:17:30,258
But we can't keep him here forever.

195
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:32,677
Oh, come on, sir.

196
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:35,305
Please, please, stop worrying so much.

197
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:36,723
GENERAL MANAGER SEOK DONG-HWAN

198
00:17:36,848 --> 00:17:38,933
I'm the youngest manager here.

199
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:42,854
I just kept him here for a few months
to see how much he knows.

200
00:17:43,646 --> 00:17:45,148
I'll deal with him soon.

201
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:48,610
So all you have to do
is sit back and decide

202
00:17:48,735 --> 00:17:51,654
whether to send him
to the Wonju Plant or the Taean Plant.

203
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:53,156
What do you think?

204
00:17:53,698 --> 00:17:54,741
The Busan Plant.

205
00:17:55,909 --> 00:17:56,826
-Damn it!
-Jeez!

206
00:18:02,290 --> 00:18:03,750
AMSEONG MUGWORT FARM CONTRACT

207
00:18:05,585 --> 00:18:06,920
I love the wheat noodles there.

208
00:18:07,045 --> 00:18:08,171
What?

209
00:18:14,427 --> 00:18:15,845
Damn it.

210
00:18:17,764 --> 00:18:20,016
PROCUREMENT ASSHOLE MANAGER JEONG YEON-HO

211
00:18:31,778 --> 00:18:33,446
What is this?

212
00:18:34,614 --> 00:18:36,324
Why aren't you answering my calls?

213
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:39,744
I called you so many times
for that unit price change report…

214
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,788
PROCUREMENT ASSISTANT MANAGER NAMGUNG HO

215
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:43,498
PROCUREMENT ASSHOLE MANAGER JEONG YEON-HO

216
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:45,583
Is that how you saved my name?

217
00:18:51,339 --> 00:18:52,340
Mr. Namgung.

218
00:18:54,217 --> 00:18:56,010
What did you save me as?

219
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,554
"Asshole Manager Jeong Yeon-ho."

220
00:18:58,555 --> 00:18:59,389
Excuse me?

221
00:18:59,514 --> 00:19:02,016
I almost used "F***ing Asshole,"

222
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:03,935
but I just went with "Asshole."

223
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:04,978
Why?

224
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:08,314
-Want me to change it?
-Mr. Namgung.

225
00:19:09,649 --> 00:19:10,984
This is insubordination.

226
00:19:11,943 --> 00:19:13,778
I'm newer, but I'm still your boss.

227
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:14,904
You can't do this.

228
00:19:15,029 --> 00:19:16,239
You think I'll just--

229
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:22,287
What are you…

230
00:19:31,546 --> 00:19:32,755
Hey, you.

231
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:34,549
Yes?

232
00:19:35,216 --> 00:19:36,551
Let me ask you this.

233
00:19:40,722 --> 00:19:44,392
Why do you think we track
imported material prices?

234
00:19:45,435 --> 00:19:46,477
Well…

235
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:48,313
That's to…

236
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:52,191
To see the price trends
from our suppliers.

237
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:55,069
For cost management

238
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:57,322
and to stay on budget.

239
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:00,617
Listen.

240
00:20:01,868 --> 00:20:03,411
We track price changes

241
00:20:03,536 --> 00:20:05,830
to check the cost structure.

242
00:20:06,748 --> 00:20:08,917
That's why we check
the raw material prices

243
00:20:09,042 --> 00:20:11,210
and exchange rates
over the last three years,

244
00:20:11,336 --> 00:20:13,171
not the shipping records.

245
00:20:14,005 --> 00:20:15,798
Well, there's also that.

246
00:20:17,342 --> 00:20:21,346
I don't care if you bully me
or run me ragged, but…

247
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,725
your sheer incompetence.

248
00:20:27,727 --> 00:20:31,272
Never, ever let me witness it.

249
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:34,108
It pisses me off.

250
00:20:39,572 --> 00:20:40,823
Shit.

251
00:20:44,285 --> 00:20:45,328
Why are you still here?

252
00:20:46,371 --> 00:20:47,538
Get out.

253
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:10,812
You see other women, too.

254
00:21:10,937 --> 00:21:12,188
It's only fair.

255
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:15,066
-Lee Mi-do.
-You do it, too.

256
00:21:17,026 --> 00:21:19,112
I won't do it if you don't.

257
00:21:23,616 --> 00:21:24,617
One week.

258
00:21:27,078 --> 00:21:28,287
I'll give you one week.

259
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:31,249
Think about it seriously.

260
00:21:41,843 --> 00:21:43,428
Go get some mudflat samples.

261
00:21:44,137 --> 00:21:45,638
Salinity differs at high tide,

262
00:21:45,763 --> 00:21:49,851
so dig at least 15 centimeters deep
every 50 meters.

263
00:21:51,811 --> 00:21:52,812
Have fun with that.

264
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,957
Sir, can I ask you something?

265
00:22:13,541 --> 00:22:15,668
I'm here to collect mudflat samples.

266
00:22:16,210 --> 00:22:17,962
Do I go that way?

267
00:22:18,087 --> 00:22:20,548
Yes, you just head straight in over there.

268
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:23,551
But the terrain around there
is pretty unusual.

269
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:25,553
The tide comes in real fast.

270
00:22:25,678 --> 00:22:27,096
Be careful.

271
00:22:27,221 --> 00:22:28,306
I see, thank you.

272
00:22:35,688 --> 00:22:37,065
Wait a minute.

273
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:40,109
It's a spring tide today,
so the water will rise fast.

274
00:22:40,234 --> 00:22:42,195
I hope he'll be alright.

275
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:38,209
Should I join the union
and get hazard pay?

276
00:23:53,850 --> 00:23:55,810
Oh, man.

277
00:24:17,331 --> 00:24:19,917
But the terrain around there
is pretty unusual.

278
00:24:20,042 --> 00:24:23,212
The tide comes in real fast. Be careful.

279
00:25:19,018 --> 00:25:20,853
I'm so sorry.

280
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:25,066
EXPRESS BUS TERMINAL

281
00:25:44,543 --> 00:25:45,795
We've met before.

282
00:25:47,964 --> 00:25:49,131
TF TEAM 3, PARK SU-A

283
00:25:50,549 --> 00:25:53,302
I'm Park Su-a of TF Team 3.

284
00:26:00,476 --> 00:26:02,353
As I mentioned on the phone,

285
00:26:03,479 --> 00:26:05,648
Mr. Namgung was
collecting samples for salinity

286
00:26:05,773 --> 00:26:07,858
when the tide rushed in,

287
00:26:08,776 --> 00:26:11,362
causing the accident.

288
00:26:12,488 --> 00:26:14,282
The accident was reported at 11:23 a.m.

289
00:26:15,032 --> 00:26:16,575
The search began at 12:00 p.m.

290
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:19,370
Currently, two coastal rescue boats

291
00:26:19,495 --> 00:26:23,416
and two search drones
are searching a 5 km radius.

292
00:26:25,167 --> 00:26:28,337
Procurement is currently in a meeting
with the director,

293
00:26:28,462 --> 00:26:30,089
so I was sent ahead.

294
00:26:31,674 --> 00:26:33,926
Once the company forms a response team,

295
00:26:34,552 --> 00:26:37,013
the executives will come down even at dawn

296
00:26:37,138 --> 00:26:39,682
-to oversee--
-That is not happening.

297
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,894
Why is the radius only 5 km?

298
00:26:44,812 --> 00:26:47,690
That boy who went missing
in Sokcho last month

299
00:26:47,815 --> 00:26:50,443
was found 20 km away
in less than three hours.

300
00:26:51,277 --> 00:26:54,989
That was a child,
so the search priorities were different.

301
00:26:55,990 --> 00:26:56,824
Right now--

302
00:26:56,949 --> 00:26:59,910
Cut the bullshit
about him just being an adult.

303
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:04,290
Hunmin Confectionery won't step up.

304
00:27:04,415 --> 00:27:05,958
Isn't that why it's dragging?

305
00:27:07,668 --> 00:27:08,544
Call someone

306
00:27:09,587 --> 00:27:12,423
who makes at least three times
what you do, right now.

307
00:27:13,299 --> 00:27:17,470
Tell them his guardian is a crazy bitch,
and she'll go to the press in 30 minutes.

308
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:20,514
That won't work.

309
00:27:24,977 --> 00:27:27,063
I already confronted them.

310
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:41,410
This guy makes five times more than I do.

311
00:27:41,535 --> 00:27:44,163
YOON DO-HAK
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR, PRODUCTION

312
00:27:46,499 --> 00:27:48,250
My complaints have no power.

313
00:27:48,376 --> 00:27:49,585
But you're different.

314
00:27:50,669 --> 00:27:52,046
Call him yourself.

315
00:27:52,755 --> 00:27:54,590
Tell him you've lost your mind…

316
00:27:56,425 --> 00:27:58,344
and will go to the press in ten.

317
00:28:01,263 --> 00:28:03,099
Say you got the card from me.

318
00:28:27,456 --> 00:28:28,374
This is Rescue.

319
00:28:28,499 --> 00:28:31,252
Missing person found
at the reef west of Sector 7.

320
00:28:48,811 --> 00:28:49,895
Dad!

321
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,441
Dad!

322
00:28:54,358 --> 00:28:55,734
Dad!

323
00:28:56,444 --> 00:28:57,987
Dad!

324
00:28:58,779 --> 00:29:01,073
Dad!

325
00:29:03,701 --> 00:29:05,744
Look! He's coming up!

326
00:29:05,870 --> 00:29:07,329
Thank goodness. He looks okay.

327
00:29:07,455 --> 00:29:09,290
What a relief.

328
00:29:10,124 --> 00:29:11,667
Goodness, I warned him earlier.

329
00:29:11,792 --> 00:29:13,294
-Oh my.
-He shouldn't have gone in.

330
00:29:13,419 --> 00:29:16,338
-He ignored the tides…
-He shouldn't have.

331
00:29:16,464 --> 00:29:17,798
Mi-do.

332
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:19,842
-Gosh.
-Oh my.

333
00:29:26,599 --> 00:29:28,184
-That fool!
-Was it Ho-sik?

334
00:29:28,851 --> 00:29:30,019
Did Ho-sik tell you?

335
00:29:32,062 --> 00:29:34,356
Eom Ho-sik, that punk.

336
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,485
-Oh my.
-Thank goodness.

337
00:29:38,569 --> 00:29:40,154
That was a close call.

338
00:29:58,130 --> 00:30:00,090
He's been missing for over an hour.

339
00:30:00,674 --> 00:30:03,135
The Procurement guys are keeping quiet.

340
00:30:04,136 --> 00:30:07,473
I'll head down after my meeting.
You go first, Ms. Park.

341
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:53,852
Deok-sun?

342
00:30:53,978 --> 00:30:54,812
Yes.

343
00:30:54,937 --> 00:30:56,981
The Haemado guesthouse owner's niece.

344
00:30:57,106 --> 00:30:59,984
Don't gossip when you don't know anything.

345
00:31:00,651 --> 00:31:02,903
Focus on your own work
instead of gossiping.

346
00:31:03,028 --> 00:31:05,447
I already confronted them.

347
00:31:36,645 --> 00:31:39,273
I got dumped by a girl
I liked for ten years,

348
00:31:39,815 --> 00:31:40,774
so I ran away.

349
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:42,026
-Ran away?
-Ran away?

350
00:31:42,151 --> 00:31:42,985
Yes.

351
00:31:43,110 --> 00:31:45,863
It hurt too much to keep seeing her.

352
00:31:50,826 --> 00:31:53,370
What's on your mind?
You didn't even see me coming.

353
00:31:54,788 --> 00:31:57,541
I had a very long day today
thanks to someone.

354
00:31:58,792 --> 00:32:00,252
Worse than mine?

355
00:32:12,890 --> 00:32:13,891
Oh.

356
00:32:17,144 --> 00:32:19,313
Don't you crave it at times like this?

357
00:32:28,447 --> 00:32:30,115
Hey, what is this?

358
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,700
Were you serious?

359
00:32:31,825 --> 00:32:32,868
Yes.

360
00:32:34,662 --> 00:32:35,496
RAVEN BLUE

361
00:32:35,621 --> 00:32:36,747
-I'm a heavy smoker.
-Hey!

362
00:32:37,623 --> 00:32:38,791
Are you crazy…

363
00:32:40,918 --> 00:32:42,795
Are you crazy? Have you lost it?

364
00:32:43,504 --> 00:32:45,130
You're too young to be smoking!

365
00:32:46,924 --> 00:32:49,301
Twenty-eight isn't exactly "too young."

366
00:32:50,219 --> 00:32:51,095
What, 28?

367
00:32:55,307 --> 00:32:56,141
You're that old?

368
00:33:05,943 --> 00:33:06,860
Anyway,

369
00:33:08,153 --> 00:33:09,196
thanks for today.

370
00:33:11,115 --> 00:33:12,950
I heard you worked hard.

371
00:33:15,911 --> 00:33:17,246
It was nothing.

372
00:33:18,288 --> 00:33:20,332
You looked after my girlfriend, too.

373
00:33:23,168 --> 00:33:25,087
I'll buy you lunch sometime.

374
00:33:26,171 --> 00:33:27,381
Get some sleep now.

375
00:33:32,052 --> 00:33:33,429
Please never do that again.

376
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:41,019
I was so scared I'd never see you again.

377
00:33:43,147 --> 00:33:45,816
I was really worried about you, so please…

378
00:33:47,985 --> 00:33:50,487
never do anything that dangerous again.

379
00:33:52,364 --> 00:33:54,199
-Never--
-Stop right there.

380
00:33:57,327 --> 00:33:59,079
Or else I can't buy you lunch.

381
00:34:03,167 --> 00:34:04,042
Go to bed.

382
00:34:18,974 --> 00:34:20,100
You're still awake?

383
00:34:20,225 --> 00:34:21,226
Yes.

384
00:34:22,186 --> 00:34:23,353
Where did you go?

385
00:34:23,479 --> 00:34:24,855
Just outside.

386
00:34:24,980 --> 00:34:27,191
I didn't get to thank Su-a earlier.

387
00:34:30,110 --> 00:34:31,111
That's her, right?

388
00:34:31,987 --> 00:34:33,322
Ssuk from Haemado.

389
00:34:33,447 --> 00:34:35,324
The one you saw again at work.

390
00:34:35,449 --> 00:34:36,700
Yes, that's her.

391
00:34:37,367 --> 00:34:38,577
She looks like Ssuk, right?

392
00:34:41,580 --> 00:34:42,539
She really does.

393
00:34:49,254 --> 00:34:50,464
I'm sorry.

394
00:34:52,466 --> 00:34:53,884
Why are you sorry?

395
00:34:54,009 --> 00:34:56,386
The call must've scared you.

396
00:35:00,349 --> 00:35:01,767
And you hate the ocean.

397
00:35:04,603 --> 00:35:06,563
Who else would've come?

398
00:35:07,523 --> 00:35:09,107
That half-wit Lee Yeong-do?

399
00:35:09,650 --> 00:35:10,984
That idiot Lee Wan-do?

400
00:35:13,362 --> 00:35:15,531
Aren't you being too mean
to your brothers?

401
00:35:21,036 --> 00:35:24,289
Let's go to sleep.
We have to head up early tomorrow.

402
00:35:31,672 --> 00:35:32,506
Okay.

403
00:35:54,194 --> 00:35:55,863
Call me when you get there.

404
00:36:00,826 --> 00:36:02,035
Mi-do.

405
00:36:03,203 --> 00:36:05,581
I hate it too, but what choice do I have?

406
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:09,251
The big boss paying my salary
told me to finish up here.

407
00:36:09,918 --> 00:36:11,628
I can stay here with you.

408
00:36:11,753 --> 00:36:12,713
No, you can't.

409
00:36:14,798 --> 00:36:16,300
You hate the ocean.

410
00:36:18,468 --> 00:36:21,054
Seeing you struggle
stresses me out even more.

411
00:36:24,683 --> 00:36:25,726
Is Park Su-a

412
00:36:26,602 --> 00:36:27,603
staying with you?

413
00:36:29,062 --> 00:36:30,063
They told her to.

414
00:36:31,023 --> 00:36:31,899
You know, right?

415
00:36:34,651 --> 00:36:37,779
You know that Su-a has feelings for you.

416
00:36:47,748 --> 00:36:49,750
I haven't done anything wrong.

417
00:36:50,626 --> 00:36:51,627
And as for her,

418
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:53,879
she's just a high schooler I knew.

419
00:36:54,463 --> 00:36:57,007
Now she's just a junior colleague.
Nothing more.

420
00:36:58,216 --> 00:36:59,801
I never led her on, either.

421
00:37:00,594 --> 00:37:01,762
You have one day left.

422
00:37:06,391 --> 00:37:08,352
I said you should see other people.

423
00:37:10,729 --> 00:37:12,397
You agreed to think about it.

424
00:37:13,523 --> 00:37:15,150
You only have one more day.

425
00:37:20,822 --> 00:37:22,532
The bus is leaving. Get on.

426
00:37:29,456 --> 00:37:30,624
Damn it.

427
00:37:32,084 --> 00:37:34,294
-Excuse me, where's Mr. Namgung?
-Huh?

428
00:37:34,962 --> 00:37:37,923
Oh, he left for the mudflats ages ago.

429
00:37:38,048 --> 00:37:41,176
He took his girlfriend
to the bus bright and early.

430
00:37:41,301 --> 00:37:42,886
He's an early bird.

431
00:37:46,348 --> 00:37:47,182
Damn it.

432
00:38:19,923 --> 00:38:21,717
Hey, what about your bus?

433
00:38:21,842 --> 00:38:24,219
You didn't send me off
because you were worried.

434
00:38:24,761 --> 00:38:26,513
You did it because I'm a pain.

435
00:38:27,097 --> 00:38:28,724
Where is this coming from?

436
00:38:36,064 --> 00:38:37,691
Is it because of Su-a?

437
00:38:40,277 --> 00:38:41,611
I told you, she's just--

438
00:38:41,737 --> 00:38:42,571
I know.

439
00:38:43,196 --> 00:38:44,698
She means nothing to you.

440
00:38:44,823 --> 00:38:46,575
It's not about her for me, either.

441
00:38:49,536 --> 00:38:50,787
Procurement.

442
00:38:52,205 --> 00:38:53,707
You moved to Procurement.

443
00:38:55,292 --> 00:38:56,668
Why didn't you tell me?

444
00:38:56,793 --> 00:38:57,627
Why?

445
00:38:57,753 --> 00:38:59,463
Because I'd worry again?

446
00:39:01,798 --> 00:39:02,799
I'm sorry.

447
00:39:04,843 --> 00:39:07,637
-I was going to--
-When you quit art,

448
00:39:08,930 --> 00:39:12,309
or when your credit was ruined
because of Aunt Hwa-young,

449
00:39:12,434 --> 00:39:15,520
or when you gave away
your entire lease deposit,

450
00:39:16,229 --> 00:39:18,607
or even when you gave her your kidney,

451
00:39:19,316 --> 00:39:20,817
you never told me.

452
00:39:21,401 --> 00:39:23,570
For the very touching reason
that I'd worry.

453
00:39:26,740 --> 00:39:28,825
Because I didn't want to be a burden.

454
00:39:31,745 --> 00:39:34,122
It was my problem,
so I had to handle it myself.

455
00:39:34,247 --> 00:39:35,290
But I know…

456
00:39:36,625 --> 00:39:38,502
that it hurt you deeply.

457
00:39:41,797 --> 00:39:42,923
I'm sorry.

458
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:45,342
It's all my fault.

459
00:39:46,134 --> 00:39:47,552
Are you really sorry?

460
00:39:50,055 --> 00:39:51,807
No, you're not.

461
00:39:51,932 --> 00:39:53,350
You're not sorry at all.

462
00:39:55,852 --> 00:39:57,104
Namgung.

463
00:39:58,855 --> 00:40:01,316
I've known you for 28 years,
since we were seven.

464
00:40:02,275 --> 00:40:03,944
I can see it in your eyes.

465
00:40:04,569 --> 00:40:06,321
Maybe not everything,

466
00:40:06,947 --> 00:40:09,825
but at least if things are good
or bad for you,

467
00:40:09,950 --> 00:40:10,867
and also…

468
00:40:12,786 --> 00:40:16,081
how you see me and what you think of me.

469
00:40:16,206 --> 00:40:17,207
I know everything.

470
00:40:20,377 --> 00:40:22,337
You think I'm despicable.

471
00:40:22,462 --> 00:40:24,005
You absolutely hate me!

472
00:40:26,049 --> 00:40:27,676
Where is this coming from?

473
00:40:27,801 --> 00:40:29,010
Damn it.

474
00:40:30,303 --> 00:40:31,680
Hey!

475
00:40:32,639 --> 00:40:33,974
Mi-do!

476
00:40:40,355 --> 00:40:42,357
I don't know what got into you,

477
00:40:42,983 --> 00:40:45,110
but I don't want to fight with you.

478
00:40:45,235 --> 00:40:46,361
Just go home.

479
00:40:46,486 --> 00:40:47,571
Damn it!

480
00:40:49,906 --> 00:40:50,949
Are you crazy…

481
00:40:52,993 --> 00:40:55,620
Did you really tell me to see that guy

482
00:40:55,745 --> 00:40:57,789
purely for my sake?

483
00:40:58,623 --> 00:40:59,583
No, it wasn't.

484
00:41:00,167 --> 00:41:02,419
You just said it to hurt me.

485
00:41:03,336 --> 00:41:06,673
Sure, maybe 90% of it was for my sake.

486
00:41:06,798 --> 00:41:08,008
You probably meant it.

487
00:41:08,842 --> 00:41:10,594
But what about the other 10%?

488
00:41:10,719 --> 00:41:12,971
Was that 10% really for me too?

489
00:41:13,847 --> 00:41:16,516
You didn't think it would hurt me
when you said that?

490
00:41:17,893 --> 00:41:20,437
Answer me!

491
00:41:28,236 --> 00:41:29,321
Yes, you're right.

492
00:41:30,197 --> 00:41:31,948
I said it to hurt you.

493
00:41:32,073 --> 00:41:32,908
Happy now?

494
00:41:39,206 --> 00:41:40,165
What?

495
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:43,501
Am I not allowed?

496
00:41:44,502 --> 00:41:47,714
Should I let you drag me along,
worrying that you'll dump me?

497
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:50,926
I'm scared of being a burden.

498
00:41:51,468 --> 00:41:52,761
Of ruining your life.

499
00:41:52,886 --> 00:41:54,763
My life is already so pathetic,

500
00:41:54,888 --> 00:41:57,224
and dealing with everything alone
is suffocating.

501
00:41:58,266 --> 00:42:00,352
But still,

502
00:42:01,061 --> 00:42:02,938
I kept living because of you.

503
00:42:04,356 --> 00:42:07,442
You're the reason I fought to survive!

504
00:42:08,109 --> 00:42:09,945
How could you do this to me?

505
00:42:11,988 --> 00:42:14,282
How could you say
he made your heart flutter

506
00:42:15,158 --> 00:42:17,535
and that he lit up your life?

507
00:42:20,121 --> 00:42:23,208
You should've flat-out denied it
even when I asked.

508
00:42:24,292 --> 00:42:25,835
You should've sworn it wasn't true.

509
00:42:27,170 --> 00:42:29,381
Then I would've let it slide.

510
00:42:29,506 --> 00:42:32,133
I would've just looked the other way!

511
00:42:32,259 --> 00:42:34,427
I didn't because I knew you'd do that!

512
00:42:35,637 --> 00:42:37,430
But you shouldn't have to.

513
00:42:37,555 --> 00:42:39,307
I already feel so sorry for you,

514
00:42:39,432 --> 00:42:41,393
and I just ended up hurting you more.

515
00:42:41,977 --> 00:42:43,645
I caused you even more pain.

516
00:42:44,938 --> 00:42:47,107
So why are you holding it in again?

517
00:42:48,233 --> 00:42:49,693
I'm just a terrible bitch.

518
00:42:49,818 --> 00:42:51,861
Why are you holding it in? Why?

519
00:42:53,113 --> 00:42:54,114
Namgung.

520
00:42:54,948 --> 00:42:57,033
You shouldn't hold it in like that.

521
00:42:57,158 --> 00:42:59,452
You're supposed to swear and get mad!

522
00:43:19,139 --> 00:43:20,765
What do you want me to do?

523
00:43:21,308 --> 00:43:24,686
I know you don't let go
once you're fixated on something.

524
00:43:25,645 --> 00:43:28,898
Then what should I do?
What was I supposed to do?

525
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:32,986
You should've said we'd try together.

526
00:43:33,695 --> 00:43:35,697
Not tell me to go see that guy.

527
00:43:36,448 --> 00:43:40,201
Even if it's miserable for both of us,

528
00:43:40,327 --> 00:43:42,329
you should've said we'd try anyway.

529
00:43:45,081 --> 00:43:46,875
But you didn't want to.

530
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:49,002
You just wanted to hurt me.

531
00:43:52,047 --> 00:43:54,382
You want to be 90% caring and 10% hurtful?

532
00:43:55,133 --> 00:43:56,801
I'm sick of it.

533
00:43:57,427 --> 00:43:59,304
Your consideration and kindness

534
00:43:59,429 --> 00:44:01,014
are suffocating me, too!

535
00:44:02,974 --> 00:44:05,101
If you want to hurt me, be 100% hurtful.

536
00:44:06,019 --> 00:44:09,647
If it's from you, I'll gladly take it.

537
00:44:10,523 --> 00:44:12,108
So give me 100%.

538
00:44:26,706 --> 00:44:27,999
I'm back.

539
00:44:28,124 --> 00:44:31,002
What? Are you back already?

540
00:44:35,131 --> 00:44:36,132
What?

541
00:44:47,143 --> 00:44:48,895
When I'm back in Seoul,

542
00:44:50,772 --> 00:44:53,108
I'll ask him to date me for a month.

543
00:44:54,901 --> 00:44:56,528
You should date that girl, too.

544
00:45:05,537 --> 00:45:07,080
You were right.

545
00:45:15,713 --> 00:45:16,798
With you,

546
00:45:18,675 --> 00:45:20,635
I feel like I could go anywhere.

547
00:45:23,263 --> 00:45:25,056
I'd be scared on my own.

548
00:45:27,559 --> 00:45:28,977
But wherever it is,

549
00:45:31,271 --> 00:45:33,189
I think I could go there with you.

550
00:46:05,555 --> 00:46:08,892
We deceive and lie to ourselves
countless times.

551
00:46:10,685 --> 00:46:13,229
Saying it's to protect the other person,

552
00:46:13,855 --> 00:46:15,482
that we'd gladly make sacrifices.

553
00:46:17,358 --> 00:46:19,569
But behind that 90% of sincerity,

554
00:46:19,694 --> 00:46:21,988
is the plain truth really so noble?

555
00:46:24,699 --> 00:46:27,577
We give the other person 90%,

556
00:46:28,328 --> 00:46:31,289
and maybe protect ourselves
with the remaining 10%.

557
00:46:32,290 --> 00:46:33,541
But Namgung,

558
00:46:34,375 --> 00:46:36,836
give me 100% now, not 10%.

559
00:46:37,712 --> 00:46:40,256
All the sorrow you felt because of me,

560
00:46:40,381 --> 00:46:44,052
the anger, the frustration, the contempt.

561
00:46:44,177 --> 00:46:46,054
Give it all back to me 100%.

562
00:46:46,888 --> 00:46:52,227
Whatever it is,
I'll gladly take it if it's from you.

563
00:46:53,186 --> 00:46:54,729
I'll accept it all.

564
00:47:50,910 --> 00:47:52,579
Did you two fight?

565
00:47:54,706 --> 00:47:56,374
Is that why you came back?

566
00:47:59,377 --> 00:48:01,504
He already went through a lot yesterday…

567
00:48:05,633 --> 00:48:07,510
No, I meant…

568
00:48:08,761 --> 00:48:09,887
We still have work.

569
00:48:10,013 --> 00:48:12,140
If you let personal issues affect work,

570
00:48:12,265 --> 00:48:13,933
then I'm the one who suffers--

571
00:48:14,058 --> 00:48:15,393
I see right through you.

572
00:48:16,936 --> 00:48:18,730
No need to try so hard.

573
00:48:24,193 --> 00:48:25,987
There's nothing between him and me.

574
00:48:30,742 --> 00:48:32,619
I think you fought because of me.

575
00:48:33,453 --> 00:48:35,163
It's just a crush on my end.

576
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:37,707
He doesn't even know I like him.

577
00:48:41,461 --> 00:48:44,255
It wasn't because of you.
It was because of me.

578
00:48:47,842 --> 00:48:49,719
I had feelings for another man.

579
00:48:53,640 --> 00:48:56,768
HAEDAM 1-RI TOWN BUS

580
00:49:04,984 --> 00:49:08,029
The survival of our company
depends on this lawsuit.

581
00:49:08,946 --> 00:49:09,781
Since Jaekang…

582
00:49:09,906 --> 00:49:10,865
DAEGONG TRADING DIR. GI

583
00:49:10,990 --> 00:49:12,325
…suddenly took their case…

584
00:49:12,450 --> 00:49:14,202
I don't doubt you, Mr. Han, but--

585
00:49:15,161 --> 00:49:16,746
I understand what you mean.

586
00:49:16,871 --> 00:49:18,081
I'll drop the case.

587
00:49:21,834 --> 00:49:25,129
But if you're up against Jaekang,
you'd be better off with me.

588
00:49:25,254 --> 00:49:27,840
I know exactly
what kind of legal strategy they'll use.

589
00:49:27,965 --> 00:49:29,384
I can already see it.

590
00:49:31,219 --> 00:49:33,012
But I won't be taking the case anymore.

591
00:49:33,888 --> 00:49:35,515
I turn down clients who doubt me.

592
00:49:42,230 --> 00:49:43,064
GI: I FEEL BAD…

593
00:49:43,189 --> 00:49:44,065
HYUNMAN: WITHDRAWING…

594
00:49:44,190 --> 00:49:45,149
HANPANG: UNFORTUNATELY…

595
00:49:45,274 --> 00:49:46,109
JEONGSE: CANCELING…

596
00:49:46,234 --> 00:49:47,652
SEORANG: DUE TO SOME ISSUES…

597
00:49:52,990 --> 00:49:54,450
DELIVERY COMPLETED

598
00:49:54,575 --> 00:49:55,576
ORDER: YUKGAEJANG

599
00:49:56,494 --> 00:49:57,370
Damn it.

600
00:50:39,078 --> 00:50:40,329
It's been over an hour.

601
00:50:41,080 --> 00:50:42,290
Must be cold by now.

602
00:50:45,084 --> 00:50:46,210
You lost weight.

603
00:50:52,008 --> 00:50:52,967
Two kilos?

604
00:51:01,267 --> 00:51:02,852
What are you doing?

605
00:51:03,644 --> 00:51:05,521
Showing up like this after three months.

606
00:51:07,356 --> 00:51:09,066
You came to see me, too.

607
00:52:18,761 --> 00:52:20,388
You've got it wrong.

608
00:52:20,513 --> 00:52:21,973
I only went there…

609
00:52:23,474 --> 00:52:24,475
Well…

610
00:52:26,561 --> 00:52:28,312
You've been going through a lot, huh?

611
00:52:31,399 --> 00:52:33,359
You've really got the wrong idea.

612
00:52:34,819 --> 00:52:38,155
My trust fund is tied up,
so I'm just staying here temporarily.

613
00:52:38,865 --> 00:52:40,366
I'll be moving soon.

614
00:52:42,869 --> 00:52:46,289
I have clients lining up to hire me…

615
00:52:51,043 --> 00:52:51,878
DONGLIM INDUSTRIES

616
00:52:52,003 --> 00:52:54,755
Attorney Han. I'm sorry,
but we'll have to cancel the retainer.

617
00:53:05,224 --> 00:53:06,225
Why are you here?

618
00:53:08,019 --> 00:53:09,854
Here to see this dumped lapdog?

619
00:53:12,565 --> 00:53:14,108
Just laugh at me instead.

620
00:53:14,233 --> 00:53:16,819
"Serves you right for being so arrogant."

621
00:53:16,944 --> 00:53:18,195
Isn't that why you came?

622
00:53:18,321 --> 00:53:21,115
Do you enjoy
belittling yourself like that?

623
00:53:25,161 --> 00:53:26,704
You're young.

624
00:53:27,413 --> 00:53:28,789
You can start over.

625
00:53:28,915 --> 00:53:30,041
Start over?

626
00:53:30,833 --> 00:53:31,959
Shit.

627
00:53:33,961 --> 00:53:35,630
How do I even do that?

628
00:53:37,298 --> 00:53:38,883
Would a total reset work?

629
00:53:39,008 --> 00:53:42,219
Who in their right mind would hire
a lawyer accused of throwing a case?

630
00:53:44,889 --> 00:53:46,432
Oh, right.

631
00:53:47,016 --> 00:53:48,351
You're the failure expert.

632
00:53:48,476 --> 00:53:50,937
Then enlighten me. What should I do?

633
00:53:51,062 --> 00:53:54,315
Be bright, positive, and confident?

634
00:53:54,440 --> 00:53:55,983
Will that help?

635
00:54:04,909 --> 00:54:07,745
Let me tell you something
as a failure expert.

636
00:54:09,372 --> 00:54:11,916
If you trip
in the middle of a crowded street

637
00:54:12,041 --> 00:54:14,001
and everyone stares at you,

638
00:54:14,710 --> 00:54:18,005
do you get up because you stay positive?
Or cheerful?

639
00:54:18,130 --> 00:54:19,048
No.

640
00:54:19,173 --> 00:54:20,925
You get up because you're embarrassed.

641
00:54:22,343 --> 00:54:26,055
I didn't get up to stay positive.
I got up because I was embarrassed.

642
00:54:27,348 --> 00:54:31,310
So if you feel embarrassed,
hurry up and get back on your feet.

643
00:54:32,144 --> 00:54:34,271
Stop wasting time on useless pride.

644
00:55:24,572 --> 00:55:26,323
Just say what's on your mind.

645
00:55:27,324 --> 00:55:29,326
You came to see me after three months,

646
00:55:29,452 --> 00:55:30,995
so you must want to talk.

647
00:55:35,750 --> 00:55:37,877
Right? Just spit it out.

648
00:55:41,797 --> 00:55:43,215
By the way,

649
00:55:45,051 --> 00:55:47,344
you knew I went to see you,

650
00:55:47,928 --> 00:55:50,765
but you didn't even look at me once.

651
00:55:51,474 --> 00:55:53,184
That's really cold.

652
00:55:53,309 --> 00:55:56,187
Were you just playing with my feelings?
Did you have fun?

653
00:56:01,734 --> 00:56:02,735
What?

654
00:56:05,488 --> 00:56:06,363
Are you crying?

655
00:56:07,031 --> 00:56:07,907
Wait, why?

656
00:56:10,910 --> 00:56:12,995
I'm the one who should be crying here.

657
00:56:13,120 --> 00:56:15,790
Look, Ms. Lee.

658
00:56:18,751 --> 00:56:19,877
Ms. Lee.

659
00:56:26,675 --> 00:56:28,427
Okay, fine.

660
00:56:28,552 --> 00:56:30,054
You can play with my feelings.

661
00:56:30,179 --> 00:56:31,430
Okay?

662
00:56:32,264 --> 00:56:33,265
Go ahead.

663
00:56:33,933 --> 00:56:35,184
I said I'm fine.

664
00:56:45,611 --> 00:56:46,987
Seo Ju-hyeok must've called you.

665
00:56:48,697 --> 00:56:49,949
Did he threaten you?

666
00:56:51,909 --> 00:56:53,452
What did he say?

667
00:56:53,577 --> 00:56:54,787
What happened?

668
00:56:58,749 --> 00:56:59,792
It's okay.

669
00:57:00,626 --> 00:57:01,836
Tell me.

670
00:57:02,670 --> 00:57:03,754
Okay?

671
00:57:12,805 --> 00:57:14,348
If…

672
00:57:17,351 --> 00:57:18,811
purely hypothetically…

673
00:57:21,147 --> 00:57:23,149
between you and my boyfriend,

674
00:57:24,650 --> 00:57:27,319
if I had to sleep with only one of you,

675
00:57:29,196 --> 00:57:31,365
I'd think about it for a week

676
00:57:32,408 --> 00:57:33,868
and sleep with you.

677
00:57:41,208 --> 00:57:44,670
But if I had to save one of you,

678
00:57:46,922 --> 00:57:50,050
I'd save my boyfriend
without a second thought.

679
00:57:55,472 --> 00:57:56,599
Wow.

680
00:57:59,101 --> 00:58:00,477
Unbelievable.

681
00:58:05,774 --> 00:58:07,193
Do you think I'm that easy?

682
00:58:08,527 --> 00:58:10,571
Tell me, am I a joke?

683
00:58:21,248 --> 00:58:23,542
But if you're okay with that…

684
00:58:25,211 --> 00:58:26,921
if it doesn't matter to you…

685
00:58:30,382 --> 00:58:32,009
would you go out with me?

686
00:58:40,684 --> 00:58:41,769
Just for a month…

687
00:58:44,230 --> 00:58:46,357
do you want to go crazy with me?

688
00:59:11,757 --> 00:59:13,759
That lady got these for us earlier.

689
00:59:26,105 --> 00:59:28,941
These are the only ice pops I've eaten
since I was seven.

690
00:59:31,193 --> 00:59:32,403
Excluding samples.

691
00:59:35,447 --> 00:59:37,324
The original flavor is the best.

692
00:59:46,166 --> 00:59:48,502
My ringback tone's been
"On the Street" for 20 years.

693
00:59:51,338 --> 00:59:52,548
So everyone thinks

694
00:59:53,799 --> 00:59:56,176
I love Sung Si-kyung.

695
00:59:57,928 --> 01:00:00,264
But that's the only song of his I know.

696
01:00:04,059 --> 01:00:05,394
In high school,

697
01:00:07,354 --> 01:00:10,566
Bus 5019 was the only one
that went from my house to school.

698
01:00:11,442 --> 01:00:12,776
But in 11th grade,

699
01:00:14,570 --> 01:00:17,406
at a bus stop ten minutes further away,

700
01:00:18,282 --> 01:00:20,659
they added a new route, Bus 8848.

701
01:00:21,660 --> 01:00:26,040
Even though walking ten more minutes
would get me to school 20 minutes earlier,

702
01:00:27,374 --> 01:00:28,959
I only took Bus 5019.

703
01:00:31,754 --> 01:00:34,173
I thought it was because I was used to it.

704
01:00:35,758 --> 01:00:37,259
But looking back…

705
01:00:40,179 --> 01:00:41,805
I think I was scared.

706
01:00:45,684 --> 01:00:47,394
Of taking a path I didn't know.

707
01:00:52,191 --> 01:00:53,692
That I might get lost.

708
01:00:57,154 --> 01:00:59,365
And never find my way back.

709
01:01:03,702 --> 01:01:06,705
Why are you suddenly telling me this?

710
01:01:10,542 --> 01:01:11,877
I'm suddenly curious.

711
01:01:15,297 --> 01:01:16,715
Bus 8848.

712
01:01:19,009 --> 01:01:21,220
Where would it have taken me?

713
01:01:22,763 --> 01:01:24,473
If I hadn't taken Bus 5019,

714
01:01:25,891 --> 01:01:28,477
could I still have gone anywhere?

715
01:01:31,897 --> 01:01:33,399
Would it have been okay?

716
01:01:37,945 --> 01:01:39,905
Actually, I'm not curious, per se.

717
01:01:43,867 --> 01:01:45,786
It's more like I want to be curious.

718
01:01:50,207 --> 01:01:51,583
So I was wondering.

719
01:01:55,337 --> 01:01:57,131
Can I be curious about you?

720
01:02:05,264 --> 01:02:07,057
What if I said it's okay?

721
01:02:09,977 --> 01:02:11,895
Would you date me for just a month?

722
01:02:56,857 --> 01:02:58,108
Just one month.

723
01:02:58,233 --> 01:03:00,694
Let's do our best with our new partners.

724
01:03:00,819 --> 01:03:02,529
How much touching is allowed?

725
01:03:02,654 --> 01:03:03,989
How much can you tolerate?

726
01:03:04,114 --> 01:03:07,159
I'll quit for real.
I'm never doing film ever again!

727
01:03:07,284 --> 01:03:08,327
Director Lee Mi-do?

728
01:03:08,452 --> 01:03:10,329
If you date me,
you'll never go back to him.

729
01:03:10,454 --> 01:03:12,664
I'll do everything I can to win you over.

730
01:03:12,789 --> 01:03:14,291
Hello. My name is Sol.

731
01:03:14,416 --> 01:03:16,835
You're here about Sol's custody, right?

732
01:03:16,960 --> 01:03:19,755
If it were your father,

733
01:03:19,880 --> 01:03:21,924
would you still save Namgung Ho?

734
01:03:24,635 --> 01:03:26,595
Subtitle translation by Cayle Kim
